  "report_summary": "Ultrasound of the right axilla with US-guided FNA and marker clip insertion, performed on [redacted]. Two slightly thickened right axillary lymph nodes with cortical thickness up to 3.5 mm were seen overlying the right axillary bundle; one was targeted for four FNA passes under local anaesthetic with samples sent to cytology. A marker clip was deployed immediately superior to the targeted node due to its proximity to the axillary bundle, with the surgical team present. No immediate complications. Right axilla graded U3."
